# Portfolio conventions

Astro 5 (SSR via the Vercel adapter) + React 19 islands + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui
+ MDX. Package manager is **pnpm**. Node >= 22.

`CLAUDE.md` at the repo root is the long-form version of this file. Read it when
you need detail this rule does not cover. `docs/design/design-system.md` is the
design system spec and outranks any styling instinct you have.

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` — local dev server.
- `pnpm build` — runs `generate:pdf` then `astro build`.
- `pnpm generate:pdf` — regenerates the gitignored CV PDFs.
- There is **no test runner**. `pnpm test` is a placeholder. Verify by running
  the app, not by claiming types pass.

## Rendering model

Pages are `.astro` and render on the server. Interactive pieces are React
islands, hydrated per use with a `client:*` directive. **Never assume a `.tsx`
component is hydrated** — check for the directive. Some islands are wrapped in a
`*Island.astro` file so MDX imports the wrapper, not the raw component.

Prefer a static `.astro` component. Reach for an island only when the reader
must manipulate something.

## Content collections

`notes` (MDX), `series` (JSON), `work` (MDX), `testimonials` (JSON). Always
filter note listings with `({ data }) => !data.draft`.

## Do not

- Do not add backwards-compat shims, `_unused` renames, or `// removed` comments.
- Do not write multi-paragraph comments explaining *what* the code does.
- Do not edit an ADR whose status is `Accepted`. Propose a superseding one.
- Do not touch `src/legacy/` — it is a frozen renderer with two known consumers.
- Do not touch `deprecated-nextjs/` — it is a dead prior implementation.
- Do not run `git reset --hard`, force-push, or delete branches.
- Do not widen the scope of your ticket. If you find unrelated breakage, note it
  in your report and leave it alone.
